  "art.1.content": {"en": "In the early hours of 2 January 1921, the mouth of the Ría de Arousa was the scene of one of the greatest naval disasters of the 20th century on the Spanish coast, but also of the most moving testimony of community solidarity recorded on the Atlantic shores. The mail steamer *Santa Isabel*, flagship of the Compañía Transatlántica Española, was en route to Buenos Aires, making stops for Galician migrant passengers.\n\n### I. The Bathymetric Trap of the Bajos de Pegar\n\nThat winter, Galicia was battered by an unrelenting succession of south-westerly fronts. At 01:50 in the morning, under dense fog and hurricane-force winds that blurred the light signals from the lighthouses of Corrubedo and Sálvora, the ship miscalculated its position while attempting to seek shelter in the estuary.\n\nAt cruising speed, the keel collided with the submerged granite needles of the **Bajos de Pegar**, less than two hundred metres from the southern coast of Sálvora. The impact tore the hull beneath the boiler rooms; the vessel was plunged into darkness, listing and split in two on the breakers with 268 souls at the mercy of waves over seven metres high.\n\n### II. The Heroines of Sálvora: Courage in a Wooden Dornilla\n\nWith most of the adult men on the mainland, four young island women took the initiative: **María Fernández Oujo, Josefa Parada, Cipriana Oujo Maneiro, and Cipriana Crujeiras**.\n\nThey launched a humble wooden *dornilla* without a deck, propelled solely by the strength of oars. In the pitch-black night, dodging sharp rocks and suction countercurrents, they completed three successive trips between the wreckage and the beach of Pazo, rescuing 56 survivors by sheer rowing effort.\n\n### III. Nautical Memory and Custody of the National Park\n\nThe Royal Society for the Rescue of Shipwrecked Persons awarded the rowers the gold medal, recognising one of the greatest civilian feats in the history of the merchant navy. That event transformed the regulations for buoyage and radiotelegraphy in the estuaries.\n\nToday, the Island of Sálvora is part of the **Maritime-Terrestrial National Park of the Atlantic Islands of Galicia**. Its pristine sands, century-old lighthouse, and rocky outcrops are now a biological sanctuary where protected colonies of shag and sea otter breed under a strict regime of regulated visits.", "gl": "Na madrugada do 2 de xaneiro de 1921, a boca da Ría de Arousa foi escenario dunha das maiores catástrofes navais do século XX no litoral español, pero tamén do testemuño de solidariedade comunitaria máis conmovedor rexistrado nas costas atlánticas. O vapor-correo *Santa Isabel*, buque insignia da Compañía Transatlántica Española, navegaba con rumbo final a Bos Aires realizando escalas de pasaxe migratorio galego.\n\n### I. A trampa batimétrica dos Baixos de Pegar\n\nAquel inverno azoutaba Galicia cunha sucesión ininterrompida de frontes do suroeste. Á 01:50 da madrugada, baixo unha néboa pechada e ventos furacanados que desdibuxaban os sinais lumínicos dos faros de Corrubedo e Sálvora, o buque calculou erradamente a súa posición ao intentar tomar abrigo na ría.\n\nA velocidade de cruceiro, a quilla colisionou contra as agullas de granito mergulladas dos **Baixos de Pegar**, a menos de douscentos metros da costa meridional de Sálvora. O impacto desgarróu o casco baixo as salas de caldeiras; a nave quedou somerxida na escuridade, escorada e partida en dous sobre a rompente con 268 almas á mercé de ondas de máis de sete metros.\n\n### II. As Heroínas de Sálvora: coraxe nunha dornilla de madeira\n\nCoa maioría dos homes adultos en terra firme, catro mozas illás tomaron a iniciativa: **María Fernández Oujo, Josefa Parada, Cipriana Oujo Maneiro e Cipriana Crujeiras**.\n\nBotaron unha humilde *dornilla* de madeira sen cuberta impulsada unicamente a remo de forza. No medio da noite cega, esquivando rochas afiadas e contracorrentes de succión, completaron tres viaxes sucesivas entre os restos do naufraxio e a praia do Pazo, rescatando a pulso de remo a 56 superviventes.\n\n### III. Memoria náutica e custodia do Parque Nacional\n\nA Real Sociedade de Salvamento de Náufragos condecorou ás remeiras coa medalla de ouro, recoñecendo unha das maiores fazañas civís na historia da mariña mercante. Aquel suceso transformou a regulamentación de balizamento e radiotelegrafía nas rías.\n\nNa actualidade, a Illa de Sálvora forma parte do **Parque Nacional Marítimo-Terrestre das Illas Atlánticas de Galicia**. Os seus areais virxes, o faro centenario e os seus rochedos son hoxe un santuario biolóxico onde crían colonias protexidas de corvo mariño cristado e lontra mariña baixo un estrito réxime de visitas reguladas."},
  "art.1.date": {"en": "Autumn 2026", "gl": "Outono 2026"},
  "art.1.excerpt": {"en": "Historical analysis of the night of 2 January 1921 at the mouth of the Ría de Arousa. The rescue by the heroines of Sálvora, the hydrography of the Pegar shoals, and the current conservation regime of the archipelago.", "gl": "Análise histórica da noite do 2 de xaneiro de 1921 na boca da Ría de Arousa. O rescate das heroínas de Sálvora, a hidrografía dos baixos de Pegar e o réxime actual de conservación do arquipélago."},
